{
  "_help": [
    "Thresholds come ONLY from D2 (Inputs (Thresholds) json → D2 header json → D2 limit column). There are no default thresholds: no D2 threshold → threshold_value / breach_flag / road_condition NULL and the DQ 'threshold' check FAILs for that defect + standard.",
    "All Good / Fair / Poor ranges and label texts used by the silver layer (thresholds come from D2). Edit here; no code change.",
    "  operator ('>' or '>=') is the breach_flag operator when D2 'Inputs (Thresholds)' column B gives none.",
    "  Classification ranges never change the breach operator.",
    "severity_ranges: CALCULATE severity where D4 has no Visual Condition (10 m) and at 100 m / 1 km (from the aggregated value).",
    "rating_ranges: CALCULATE rating_ca (CA ranges + CA threshold) and rating_irc (IRC ranges + IRC threshold) at every level,",
    "rating_ca / rating_irc: 10 m → D4 Visual Condition (CA → rating_ca, IRC → rating_irc) as it is; if D4 has none → calculated. 100 m → calculated from the aggregated 10 m values; 1 km → calculated from the aggregated 100 m values. Threshold = D2 of that standard only (no defaults; not in D2 → calculated label NULL). Rutting, roughness, ravelling, cracking.",
    "  from that level's own value (10 m value; 100 m / 1 km aggregated value).",
    "Band format (checked in order, first match wins):",
    "  'to' = fixed upper limit, or 'to_ratio' = ratio × threshold of that standard; 'round': true rounds that limit (old notebook);",
    "  'to_inclusive': true → value <= limit, else value < limit; the last band has no limit.",
    "  'text' = label written to the table; {from} = previous band's limit, {to} = this band's limit (old notebook style 'Good (<10mm)').",
    "Boundaries follow the old notebook: rutting / roughness Fair <= T, Poor > T; ravelling Fair < T, Poor >= T.",
    "Values: rutting mm, roughness BI mm/km (never IRI m/km), ravelling % of the 35 sq m lane (area sq m × 100 / 35).",
    "project_overrides: { '<UPC folder or UPC>': { any section above } } is merged over these settings for that project only.",
    "_source fields say where each number comes from."
